s to determine we are out for  consultation at the moment we've just  been consulting on the the nhs page  on  well an indicative ballot it's called um  so it's not a formal industrial action  ballot uh which as you know is very  restrictive because of the legislation  that we've got um so we are but we're  consulting across loads of sectors so  our local government sector health  sector or police staff members uh all  being consulted on what they think about  the offer or lack of an offer that  they've been that they've been given  where will it lead i don't know yet at  this point in time for example in the  nhs  there are 16 trade unions and i used to  be the lead negotiator for those unions  so i know how difficult it is to get  consent is across them but that's the  aim is to actually talk to the other  unions in each of the sectors where  we're the main union and see how far we  can go down the road of getting some  consensus for  a plan of action shall we say going  forward  you are i think probably the first woman  leader of unison if i'm not mistaken 75  percent of your members are women that  reflects a wider  trend in the trade union movement which  is now  has more women members and  leader of the tc is a woman and so on  do you think that is going to lead to a  change in the tactics and indeed the  preoccupations the agenda of the trade  union movement  i think it will present a different  image of the trade union movement  without a doubt as in i think uh  people will see us perhaps differently  than you know  and i'm not  saying all leaders wear the kind of tub  thumping type of uh traditional image of  of a trade union leader i mean by no  means our male trade union leaders all  like that  but so to interrupt you but it's very  interesting the i think probably the  best-selling novel of the the the year  uh richard osmond the thursday murder  club has uh you've read it and it has a  guy in it who is a retired trade union  leader who is probably a mix